tion.","Pushes a pawn towards the White king, to pry open lines in front of it.","The next best move, 51…Rxa5, would drop Black's winning chances from 90% to 75% (−2.98).","51…g3+ pushes the passed pawn to g3.","Gives check, so the reply is forced.","White answers 52.Ke1, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on g3."]}],"opening":{"name":"English Opening: Agincourt Defense","eco":"A13","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 3.Bg2: 5 moves in all, 3 by White and 2 by Black.","Black left the book with 3…Nc6. In 4,637 games from this position, strong players played 3…Nf6 (71%), 3…d4 (9%), 3…dxc4 (8%) or 3…c6 (5%).","The main line goes on 3…Nf6 4.Nf3 Be7 5.O-O O-O 6.b3 b6 7.Bb2 Bb7 8.e3.","From here White scored 52% in those games, with 16% drawn."]}}